  ('Solve a crossing constraint with a fixed trip count 1', 'A guide crosses a narrow bridge with 3 identical crates, carrying only one crate per trip. The guide starts on the near side and must finish across. How many one-way crossings are needed if each crate must be carried across once and the guide returns for the next?', '3', '4', '5', '6', 'C', 'The guide makes 3 outward crossings and returns between crates (2 returns): 5 crossings.', 'Puzzles', 'easy'),
  ('Check consistency in a one-truthful-statement puzzle 2', 'Exactly one of Ari, Bo, and Cy took a key, and exactly one statement is true. Ari says “Bo took it.” Bo says “Ari took it.” Cy says “Ari took it.” Who took the key?', 'Ari', 'Bo', 'Cy', 'No one', 'B', 'If Ari took it, two statements are true; if Cy took it, none are true. Only Bo taking it makes exactly one statement true.', 'Puzzles', 'easy'),
  ('Find the odd weight with one balance comparison 3', 'Among eight identical-looking tokens, one is heavier. What is the minimum number of balance-scale weighings needed in the worst case to identify it?', '3', '1', '4', '2', 'D', 'A first weighing of three against three identifies the heavier group or leaves the two unweighed. A second weighing resolves any group of at most three, so two are sufficient; one weighing has only three outcomes and cannot distinguish eight tokens.', 'Puzzles', 'easy'),
